The bug: in the Mul.make_args loop, `h.is_Function` is True for cos(theta) even though it doesn't involve n. Fix: only treat as y term if h.func == y.func; if it's another function but doesn't depend on n, treat as coefficient. Upstream fix (sympy commit) rewrote to collect terms using `f.collect(y.func(Wild...))` — actual fix: check `if h.func == y.func` then process; elif h.has functions of n? Actually cos(theta) has no n. Better: treat h as coefficient unless it is an applied UndefinedFunction with y.func and argument matching n+k. If h.is_Function and h.func == y.func → term. Otherwise, if h depends on n via another function → error; else coefficient.

